# Jetsam in a game of three: "each opponent mills three cards, then you may cast a spell from each opponent's graveyard" is one cast
# for each opponent's graveyard (CR 608.2g), asked graveyard by graveyard in turn order, and no more than one from each. Bot2 mills
# Lightning Bolt, Shock and an Island: Bot1 casts the Bolt free at Bot3 and is not asked about the Shock (it stays in Bot2's graveyard
# with the Island). Then Bot3 mills Grizzly Bears and two Islands: Bot1 casts the Bears, which resolve under Bot1's control. The Bolt
# is exiled as it resolves.

[Bot1 Deck]
Flotsam // Jetsam
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Island
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x7
Lightning Bolt
Shock
Island x11

[Bot3 Deck]
Island x7
Grizzly Bears
Island x11

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Flotsam // Jetsam.Cast(Ability: Jetsam)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Lightning Bolt)
Bot1.Target(Bot3)
Bot1.Choose(Grizzly Bears)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass

[Expect]
Bot3.Life = 17
Exile = Lightning Bolt
Bot2.Graveyard = Island; Shock
Bot3.Graveyard.Count = 2
Bot1.Battlefield = Grizzly Bears; Island; Mox Emerald; Mox Jet; Mox Pearl; Mox Ruby; Mox Sapphire
Stack.Count = 0
